## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple SwiftUI parity of `components/ai/AITCONarration.tsx` — the opt-in Helix **TCO narration** surface — committed as `ca36f9119`.

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AITCONarration.*`, 9 files):
- The `withAiFeature` gate → `.gated` EmptyView; the always-rendered `AIFeatureCard` body (title + "Helix" badge + long-form description + empty hint + "Ask Helix" CTA); the `AiOutputPanel` state machine (`useAiStream` → idle/thinking/text/error precedence); double-submit guard; P4 leaf chrome (freshness chip, banner, loading skeleton, retryable error).
- Bound through a P1/S8 state-holder seam (no HTTP in the view), P1/S9 tokens, P1/S10 i18n facade (web keys verbatim, zero English literals), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry. Full VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, Reduce-Motion. **35 unit tests**.
- Minimal `project.yml` wiring (2 lines) to register the new `shared-surfaces` dir in both app targets.

**Verification** (per the established P4 disposition, cf. sibling `0088-LoadingSkeleton`):
- ✅ Isolated SwiftPM build+test: **35/35 pass** under Swift 6 strict-concurrency
- ✅ iOS 18 SDK type-check of the view layer: clean
